 {r}←{compileFlag}StartHelp userMode;tno;parms;helpFilename
⍝ Puts the help on display.\\
⍝ In case `compileFlag` is 1 the help file is re-compiled. The `MarkAPL` class must be available then.
⍝ `compileFlag` defaults to 0 except when the help file cannot be found.
⍝ `userMode` is a Boolean. If it is 1 then there is no "Developer" menu. Setting `userMode`
⍝ to 1 has no effect in case `compileFlag` is 0.
 r←⍬
 helpFilename←'Help\Laguntza.dcf'
 parms←##.APLGUI.Laguntza.CreateParms ⍬
 :If 'CLEAR WS'≡⎕WSID
     :If 0<##.⎕NC'CiderConfig'
         parms.folderName←##.CiderConfig.HOME,'\Assets\Help'
     :Else
         parms.folderName←##.TatinVars.HOME CiderConfig.HOME,'\Assets\Help'
     :EndIf
 :Else
     parms.folderName←(↑⎕NPARTS ⎕WSID),'Assets\Help'
 :EndIf
 compileFlag←(parms.folderName,'/',helpFilename){0<⎕NC ⍵:⍎⍵ ⋄ 0=⎕NEXISTS ⍺}'compileFlag'
 'Right argument must be a Boolean'⎕SIGNAL 11/⍨∧/(,userMode)∘≢¨,¨0 1
 parms.helpAbout←'GUI Help' '' 'Kai Jaeger' ''('Version ',{(1⊃⍵),' from ',2⊃⍵}Version)
 parms.helpCaption←'APL GUI Help'
 parms.helpVersion←''
 parms.helpVersionDate←''
 parms.userMode←userMode
 :If compileFlag
     parms.source←⎕THIS
 :Else
     parms.userMode←1
 :EndIf
 compileFlag ##.APLGUI.Laguntza.New parms
